[
    {
        "content": "<p>I fell into a rabbit hole while thinking about disjointness of submodules, and I now have a basic conjecture about modular lattices (<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsModularLattice#doc\">docs#IsModularLattice</a>) which I am unable to prove:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Span</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">conjecture</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsModularLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_inf_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note that I have a partial result, the proof of which is quite ugly:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">partial_solution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsModularLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_extra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_inf_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">suffices</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sup_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsModularLattice</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sup_inf_sup_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_le_iff</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_sup_right</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and_true</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">sup_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inf_eq_left</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_extra</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">conv_lhs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sup_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsModularLattice</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inf_sup_inf_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_le_sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_le_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and, for sanity check, the theorem is indeed true (with an even more ugly proof) in the lattices of subgroups of an abelian group (the same proof would work for submodule ofc):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_inf_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_sup</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">obtain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨⟨</span><span class=\"n\">k₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">k₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">sub_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk₂</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_eq_add_neg</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_comm</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_mem_sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">neg_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_sup</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">obtain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">ha'K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha'</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">hb'K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb'</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">add_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb'</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddSubgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_sup</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ha'K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I feel like I'm missing something obvious.</p>",
        "id": 609407757,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783674287
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Note: I will be very sad if people feed this question to their LLM, please avoid doing so)</p>",
        "id": 609408078,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783674393
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, I should have googled before asking. It turns out this is a known fact, let me do a bit of reference hunting</p>",
        "id": 609409220,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783674753
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, no, I read too fast! What is known if that if <code>K</code> is such that <code>h</code> is true for all <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>, then the conclusion is true for all <code>A</code> and <code>B</code>. This is not what I want.</p>",
        "id": 609411332,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783675420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Okay, reference found, it appears to be a theorem by Ore.</p>",
        "id": 609412463,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783675800
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>PR? :)</p>",
        "id": 609416276,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1783677016
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I will do ! But from a quick glance at the proof it seems like I need to focus to write it correctly, which I have postponed for now <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 609416688,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783677139
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The full theorem is that if condtion <code>h</code> is satisfied, then the sublattice generated by <code>K</code>, <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> is distributive (!)</p>",
        "id": 609417085,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783677259
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that starting the proof with <code>eq_of_le_of_inf_le_of_le_sup</code> is a good idea: the second condition is easy.</p>",
        "id": 609419356,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1783677989
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>OK now I am lost in this maze of <code>inf_sup_assoc_of_le</code> and friends.</p>",
        "id": 609421753,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1783678847
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is precisely why I gave up (consider that I was doing this at 1 am last night...)</p>",
        "id": 609421865,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783678882
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Don't you think that using an LLM (or any other automated tool) would be a good idea here? I mean,  do you have an intuition of what's going on? Because personally I am just trying random lemmas until it works and I would be very happy Is a script would do the same. I would be even happier if there is something to learn of course!</p>",
        "id": 609423168,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1783679339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is why I searched for a reference: I'm sure there is a way to understand what's going on.</p>",
        "id": 609423280,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783679381
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have not checked if all the definitions line up, but it looks like this is Theorem 11 on page 78 of Birkhoff's Lattice Theory: <a href=\"https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.166886/page/78/mode/2up\">https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.166886/page/78/mode/2up</a>.</p>",
        "id": 609427199,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1783680801
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this seems like it could be some explicit computation with the free modular lattice in three generators</p>",
        "id": 609438293,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1783684749
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aaron just showed me a very short proof of the conjecture he's formalised, but his internet isn't working right now</p>",
        "id": 609475242,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1783694938
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice ! I didn’t take time to look carefully at any of the proofs in the litterature yet, I just know that the notations used by Ore seemed a bit weird. But I’m looking forward to the proof Aaron came up with !</p>",
        "id": 609475761,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783695072
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's Aaron's really nice proof:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ModularLattice</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsModularLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_dual</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux₂</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">replace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inf_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_sup_assoc_of_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_sup_left</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sup_inf_self</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inf_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aux₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">aux₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">aux₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 609477390,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1783695458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>\"I stared at the free modular lattice in three generators then wrote down the proof\"</p>",
        "id": 609477466,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1783695479
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's probably much easier to find the proof once you know that the stronger statement</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"268315\">Anatole Dedecker</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/116395-maths/topic/A.20conjecture.20about.20modular.20lattices/near/609417085\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The full theorem is that if condtion <code>h</code> is satisfied, then the sublattice generated by <code>K</code>, <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> is distributive (!)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>is true (but Aaron's proof is still very elegant!)</p>",
        "id": 609479034,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1783695886
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I was going to say that one of the missing ingredients in my attempts was probably to exchange some of the variables, which the stronger statement suggests you can do. In any case, congrats Aaron, and please open a PR when you can !</p>",
        "id": 609479658,
        "sender_full_name": "Anatole Dedecker",
        "timestamp": 1783696040
    },
    {
